          "path": "_m/g/c/9/7/ballina-railway-station-wp/ballina-station-geograph-49079.jpg",
          "filename": "Ballina Station (geograph 4907965).jpg",
          "caption": "Ballina Station. The terminus of the branch line from Manulla Junction. The Ballina line is part of the InterCity network but is usually operated by a 'suburban' class 2800 diesel multiple unit, as seen here, which provides a connecting shuttle service at Manulla Junction with InterCity trains running between Westport and Dublin Hueston. Ballina still retains rail freight facilities and has regular container and timber traffic.",
          "alt": "Ballina Station. The terminus of the branch line from Manulla Junction. The Ballina line is part of the InterCity network but is usually operated by a 'suburban' class 2800 diesel multiple unit, as seen here, which provides a connecting shuttle service at Manulla Junction with InterCity trains running between Westport and Dublin Hueston. Ballina still retains rail freight facilities and has regular container and timber traffic.",
